#
# .hypatia-ignore — scoped, documented exemptions for the Hypatia scanner.
#
# Format (one entry per line):
#     <rule_module>/<rule_type>:<path-fragment>
#     <rule_module>/*:<path-fragment>          (any type in module)
#     <path-fragment>                           (any rule, any module)
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. A path-fragment is a substring match
# against the repo-relative file path. Hypatia's built-in defaults live in
# hypatia's lib/hypatia/scanner_suppression.ex — do not duplicate them here.
# Prefer fixing the code, or an inline directive at the finding, over an entry
# in this file: this file is for whole-path exemptions only, and every entry
# must carry a stated reason.
#
# NO ENTRIES.
#
# This repository carries no exemptions because `.github/workflows/hypatia-scan.yml`
# (standards' `hypatia-scan-reusable.yml`) is green without them. The file exists
# so that the scanner's configured path is present and reviewable — a future
# exemption has to be added here, in a diff, rather than by disabling a job.
#
# History: rsr-template-repo's copy of this file carries a long SD022 exemption
# for `build/docs-seed/`, whose example paths describe a hypothetical generated
# project rather than the template itself. This repo has no docs-seed tree, so
# inheriting that exemption would suppress findings for directories that do not
# exist here — an allowlist entry whose only effect is to widen the blind spot.
# If `build/docs-seed/` is ever adopted, re-evaluate the exemption at that point
# instead of pre-approving it.
